      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Failed femoral total hip replacement components are frequently associated with bone loss. At the time of revision surgery, the goals are to create a construct that relieves pain, is stable, and preserves and enhances bone stock. This article discusses Materials and Methods, Indications, Operative Technique, and Results regarding onlay cortical allografting for the femur."},
